# Vercel needs public/ (the site), api/ (the serverless functions), and
# vercel.json + package.json. Everything else is repo, not deploy.
#
# Keep this tight: the CLI uploads every non-ignored file from your machine, so one stray
# 45 MB asset or a 17 MB scratch directory is the difference between a deploy that works
# on a normal connection and one that dies at 100%.

.git
.vscode
node_modules
extension
packages

# tooling + scratch state
.claude
.github
.vercel
.vexp
.tasktmp
.hive-relay-data

# source and docs that never reach a browser
docs
tests
web
marketing
data
brand
enterprise-test
real-test-scenario
hive-work-resolve
demo-recording*
*.md

# build artefacts and non-web files
*.vsix
*.wasm
*.mjs
*.txt
*.cpp
*.java
*.json
*.html

# the uncompressed master recording (45 MB); the site serves the 17 MB
# hivecode-icr-demo.mp4 re-encode instead
public/Hivecode___ICR.mp4

!package.json
!vercel.json
!public/index.html
!public/control.html
!public/favicon.ico
!public/favicon-32.png
!public/apple-touch-icon.png
